<title>GERMANY: BMW 1996 group sales up 13.3 pct.</title>
<headline>BMW 1996 group sales up 13.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calender year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  52,270  vs 46,144</p>
<p>    Car production (units)		 1,143,558 vs 1,098,582</p>
<p>    --of which BMW (units)		   639,433 vs 595,056</p>
<p>    --of which Rover Group (units)	 504,125 vs 503,526</p>
<p>Car deliveries to customers (units)1,151,361 vs 1,073,161</p>
<p>    --of which BMW (units)		   644,107 vs 590,072</p>
<p>    --of which Rover Group (units)	 507,254 vs 483,089</p>
<p>    Motorcycle production (units)	  48,950  vs 52,653</p>
<p>    Motorcycle deliveries (units)	  50,466  vs 50,246</p>
<p>    Workforce (headcount)		    116,112 vs 115,763</p>
<p>    Investment				   3,900   vs 3,477</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaking group is Bayerische Motoren Werke AG. The company did not report profit figures.</p>
<p>BMW also said that deliveries of its 5-series models rose by more than 50 percent in 1996 to about 190,000 cars while sales of the 3-series totalled more than 400,000.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
